---
title: Parsers & Extensions
description: Document-level parser contracts and custom update strategies.
---

## Built-in parsers

| Parser | Module | Extensions | Default strategy |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `YamlParser` | `yacla-yaml` | `yml`, `yaml` | `YamlUpdateStrategy` |
| `JsonParser` | `yacla-json` | `json` | `JsonUpdateStrategy` |

Parsers work on document maps. Object construction and annotation validation are handled separately by core.

## Parser contract

```kotlin
import net.ririfa.yacla.loader.UpdateStrategy
import java.io.InputStream
import java.io.OutputStream

interface ConfigParser {
    val supportedExtensions: Set<String>
    val defaultUpdateStrategy: UpdateStrategy?
        get() = null

    fun parse(input: InputStream): Map<String, Any?>
    fun write(output: OutputStream, config: Map<String, Any?>)
}
```

The actual interface is `net.ririfa.yacla.parser.ConfigParser`. The root must be a mapping with string keys. Supported values include null, strings, booleans, numbers, lists, and nested mappings.

Implementations must leave caller-owned streams open on success and failure. Text output uses UTF-8. The caller controls closing and flushing.

```kotlin
import net.ririfa.yacla.yaml.YamlParser
import java.nio.file.Files
import java.nio.file.Paths

Files.newOutputStream(Paths.get("export.yml")).use { output ->
    YamlParser().write(output, mapOf("version" to "1.0.0", "enabled" to true))
}
```

`write(...)` receives a document map, not an arbitrary config object. Ordinary parser writing is separate from the YAML strategy's comment-aware update path.

## Add another format

Implement `ConfigParser` using the format's document parser and writer, then select it with the loader builder's `parser(...)`. Supply extensions for localized resource resolution. Leaving `defaultUpdateStrategy` null means the format has no default update behavior.

## Custom update strategy

`net.ririfa.yacla.loader.UpdateStrategy` defines:

```kotlin
fun updateIfNeeded(context: UpdateContext): Boolean
```

`UpdateContext` is in `net.ririfa.yacla.loader.util` and provides the parser, target file, resource path, and optional logger. Return true only when the target file changed. Select your implementation with builder `updateStrategy(...)`, shared `LoaderSettings.updateStrategy`, or the parser's default property.

A manual update does not refresh `loader.config`; the caller reloads after a successful update.
